  "worked_solution": "First, let $u=1-4x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4\\,\u27f9\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe can now rewrite the integral in terms of $u,$ solve it, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{1-4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{1-4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|u|+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|1-4x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can further simplify the above by writing $C=-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061K$ for another arbitrary constant $K,$ and then we can combine the two terms using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|1-4x|+C & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|1-4x|-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061K \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|1-4x|+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061K) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(K|1-4x|)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we finally conclude that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{3}{1-4x}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(K|1-4x|).\n$$",
